  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A dense metallic shard in a close orbit, almost certainly a fragment of whatever event left the inner world bare. It is locked, airless and reflects badly, so from the ring sea below it shows as a moving gap in the stars rather than as an object. It raises the nineteen-metre tide that everything on the ring is arranged around, and its orbit is decaying slowly enough for the decay to be a research question rather than a problem.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
